    "body": "This PR adds coverage for the global PSBT version field validation on decode.\n\n`test_psbt_unsupported_version_field` checks that the PSBT has supported version number into the `PSBT_GLOBAL_VERSION` field.\nThe test can be triggered with this diff:\n<details>\n<summary>Diff</summary>\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/src/psbt.h b/src/psbt.h\nindex 5eb5e81428..d90528e01d 100644\n--- a/src/psbt.h\n+++ b/src/psbt.h\n@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ inline constexpr uint8_t PSBT_SEPARATOR = 0x00;\n inline constexpr std::streamsize MAX_FILE_SIZE_PSBT{100'000'000}; // 100 MB\n \n // PSBT version number\n-inline constexpr uint32_t PSBT_HIGHEST_VERSION = 2;\n+inline constexpr uint32_t PSBT_HIGHEST_VERSION = 4;\n \n /** A structure for PSBT proprietary types */\n struct PSBTProprietary\n```\n</details>\n\n\n`test_psbt_missing_version_field` checks that a PSBT  without the `PSBT_GLOBAL_VERSION` field is interpreted as a v0. I've created a v2 and removed the field to check the correct behavior (fails beacuse it was originally a v2 and now is misinterpreted as a v0).\nThe test can be triggered with this diff:\n<details>\n<summary>Diff</summary>\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/src/psbt.h b/src/psbt.h\nindex 5eb5e81428..ea11267e0f 100644\n--- a/src/psbt.h\n+++ b/src/psbt.h\n@@ -1515,7 +1515,7 @@ public:\n         if (psbt_ver == 0) {\n             // Make sure that we got an unsigned tx for PSBTv0\n             if (!tx) {\n-                throw std::ios_base::failure(\"No unsigned transaction was provided\");\n+                //throw std::ios_base::failure(\"No unsigned transaction was provided\");\n             }\n             // Make sure no PSBTv2 fields are present\n             if (found_tx_version) {\n```\n</details>\n\nPrior to this PR, no test would be triggered with this diffs.",
